From bc1b4953aece01c67fd7e2e0b3fda05b9a3e0f9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redux Deep Research <redux@invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:01:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] drm/panel: add GalaxyCore GC9703 driver for the RG34XX-SP
 v2 panel

Later Anbernic RG34XX-SP handhelds (board strap PE6 high) carry a
second 3.4" 720x480 panel: 24-bit parallel RGB, set up over 3-wire
SPI. Its register sequence opens with the GalaxyCore GC9703 command-set
enable (0xd7 0x61 0x74 0x97) and follows that controller's page layout
(0xd0 0x10/0x11/0x12), with parameters of up to 44 bytes, so it does
not fit the existing { cmd, val } table drivers. Add a small driver for
GC9703 panels of this kind, with this panel as its first entry.

The table is the sequence the stock Anbernic u-boot (U-Boot 2018.05)
sends for this panel, without its trailing exit-sleep and display-on,
which the driver sends. The same sequence, timing (26 MHz, 60 Hz) and
delays (10 ms reset, 50 ms before the first command, 120 ms after
exit-sleep, 120 ms before the backlight) drive this panel on mainline
in ROCKNIX (tag 20261101) through a generic table-driven panel driver.
The table was generated with tools/gen_gc9703_table.py in
Allwinner-H700-Custom-Kernel-Research from the stock image, which
checks the result against that working file.

The controller was identified from the sequence, not from a marking on
the part or a datasheet.

This patch was drafted with an AI coding assistant (Claude) and checked
by building with W=1 (arm64, gcc 13.3.0). It has not been tested on
hardware.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig                 |  11 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile                |   1 +
 .../gpu/drm/panel/panel-galaxycore-gc9703.c   | 458 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 470 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-galaxycore-gc9703.c

